              "summary": "project:fact - [tags: testing serial parallel rust nextest shared-state] Rust's default test runner runs tests in the same binary in parallel (per-binary parallelism, not cross-binary). Tests that mutate shared process-global state (env vars, statics, `std::env::set_var`) race against each other. Two patterns: (1) `serial_test` crate with `#[serial]` attribute serializes named tests; (2) a custom `Mutex` guard (kimetsu's `test_env_lock()`)."
            },
