              "summary": "project:fact - [tags: tokio select cancellation futures drop rust] `tokio::select!` cancels all other branches when one branch completes. The cancelled futures are dropped immediately, which means any state held by a cancelled future is dropped too. If a branch was in the middle of writing to a channel or acquiring a mutex, the half-completed operation is silently discarded."
