              "summary": "project:fact - [tags: rust kimetsu-brain import dedup add_memory] When implementing import dedup for `add_memory` (which returns the existing ID on a normalized-text collision), a per-call `seen_ids` set starting fresh on each `import_memories` invocation will miscount — both a first-import and a re-import appear identical to the set. The correct pattern is: (1) snapshot all pre-existing active memory IDs via a read-only query BEFORE the loop, (2) maintain a within-batch set for intra-batch dedup. Then `deduped += 1` when the returned ID is in either set; `imported += 1` otherwise."
