              "summary": "project:fact - [2026-09-07] [tags: git reflog recovery lost-commit reset] If you accidentally `git reset --hard HEAD~N` or force-push over commits, they are NOT gone — they live in the reflog for 90 days by default. Run `git reflog show HEAD` to find the lost SHA, then `git checkout -b rescue <sha>` to recover. The reflog is local only — remote reflog is not accessible via normal git commands."
