              "kind": "memory",
              "score": 0.98052579164505,
              "summary": "project:fact - [tags: tokio shutdown graceful ordering async rust] Graceful tokio shutdown requires careful ordering: (1) stop accepting new requests, (2) wait for in-flight requests to complete, (3) shut down background tasks (harvester, GC), (4) flush writes to SQLite, (5) close connections. A common mistake is shutting down the database connection pool before in-flight tasks finish their queries — the task panics when the pool returns an error. Use a `tokio::sync::broadcast` channel for the shutdown signal and a `JoinSet` to track in-flight tasks."
            }
