              "summary": "project:fact - [tags: git submodule pinning workspace kbench] Git submodules record a specific commit SHA, not a branch. Running `git submodule update --remote` advances the pinned commit to the branch tip — this is intentional only during a deliberate upgrade. In a CI pipeline, always `git submodule update --init --recursive` (without `--remote`) to get the pinned version."
