              "kind": "memory",
              "score": 0.9857924580574036,
              "summary": "project:fact - [tags: git worktrees kimetsu brain isolation] When using `git worktree add` to work on multiple branches simultaneously, each worktree shares the `.git` directory of the main checkout. kimetsu's `ProjectPaths::discover` walks up to the git root — if you run kimetsu from a worktree, it finds the SAME `.git` and therefore the SAME kimetsu brain as the main checkout. This is usually correct behavior (one brain per repo), but tests spawned from a worktree can contaminate the shared brain."
            }
          ],
